xscaleinten -- KILL TABLE 3, PRETABLE, written 2026-09-12 BEFORE the table runs.  Post-table notes go in a
SEPARATE file (POSTTABLE.out) -- an append rewrites this file's mtime, which is the order evidence.

WHY A TABLE 3.  The pass-2 panel (_scratchpad/panel_20260912_095235_xscalepass2, plus the Opus measuring seat)
found two re-introductions of the removed exit that the 29-row instrument cannot see:
  M_RD0       `if (rd == 0) { fatal; exit(1); }' after the load      -- MEASURED 29/29 by the Opus seat
              (../opus_pass2_20260912/xscale_XM_RD0.log); predicted 29/29 by codex, grok, glm, deepseek, kimi.
  M_MAGICBIT  `if (i80321_inten & 0x00400000) { fatal; exit(1); }'   -- bit 22 is one of 0x005A0FA0, the bits
              no row's inten value (0, S1, S2, bit 28) ever sets.  Opus log ../opus_pass2_20260912/xscale_XM_MAGICBIT.log.
The seats split on whether these are floor cells or clause-(e) disclosure; that is for adjudication.  The
detector is UNSHIPPED, so a row is licensed either way as L1 pre-ship construction, and ONE row fires both:
  RD0_ALLONES  fresh session: r0 <- 0xdeadbe00 (poison), r1 <- 0xffffffff; mcr inten <- r1; mrc r0 <- inten;
               want r0 == 0xffffffff.  Poison checked before the read; a wrong Rd leaves the poison.
Also corrected in the same edit (comment-only): the CONTRACT's M5 line -- the measured M5 redirects the crn-0 arm
to isteer in BOTH directions, not "the read" only (codex, grok, kimi; confirmed in mut_xscale_t2.py) -- and the
NOT COVERED list gains rd == k for undriven k, exact inten values, and isteer != 0.

INSTRUMENT: xscale_inten_probe.T3FROZEN.py (30 rows), copied from regress/ at launch; cmp-identical to regress/.
BASELINE: current SEC cpu_arm_coproc.c (the fix).  HEAD: cpu_arm_coproc.HEAD.c (committed).

PREDICTIONS (score / 30; the new row in brackets).  Every table-2 leg keeps its table-2 failures and adds nothing,
because the new session has isrc = 0, opcode1 = opcode2 = 0, rd = 0, one read per process, and reads inten:
  BASE          30/30 CONTROL=OK       [RD0_ALLONES ok]
  HEAD          12/30 CONTROL=FAIL     [FAIL: HOST-DIED at the mrc]  -- 9 FAIL + 8 BLOCKED + this 1 FAIL = 18 non-passing
  M1            27/30                  [ok: isrc == 0]
  M5            28/30                  [ok: write and read both go through isteer, round-trip all-ones]
  M_OPCODE2     27/30                  [ok: opcode2 == 0]
  M_RD15        29/30                  [ok]
  M_NREAD       27/30                  [ok: static counter is per process; one read]
  M_OP1         29/30                  [ok]
  M_ISTEER_WR   29/30                  [ok: the row reads inten, not isteer]
  M_CRM         29/30                  [ok: crm == 0]
  M_RD0         29/30                  [FAIL -- SOLE killer]
  M_MAGICBIT    29/30                  [FAIL -- SOLE killer]

CHECKS.  SIBLING PARITY -- unchanged from table 2.  CLAIM -> ROW -- the new CONTRACT sentences: "rd == 0 (M_RD0)"
and "an inten bit no other row sets (M_MAGICBIT)" -> RD0_ALLONES; the NOT COVERED additions are disclosures, no row.
GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD -- the body reads rd (as an index) and i80321_inten; it TESTS neither, which is why the
rows had pinned them only at the values they happened to use.  CHANNEL -- RD0_ALLONES reads a register value
(r0); under M_RD0 and M_MAGICBIT the host exits at the mrc, so the value never arrives -> FAIL, not BLOCKED
(the poison was observed first).  Under every other leg the channel carries 0xffffffff.
